// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// [4] GC reachability. gc.c marks vm->spill_stack[0, spill_top) -- but a
// suspended continuation's slots sit above spill_top, and its snapshot (once
// there is one) is not the VM's array at all. Spilled locals holding heap
// objects therefore have no root while the continuation waits, so a collection
// frees them and the resumed body reads through dangling pointers.
//
// The strings are built at run time by concatenation so they are genuine heap
// objects rather than chunk constants, which the constant table would keep
// alive regardless and hide the defect. Only the spilled slots need to hold
// one; everything below the cap is an ordinary number.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
func mk(s) { return "obj-" + s }

